@/chart

## 8. Quick Revision Table

| Measure | Formula | Key sign reading |
| --- | --- | --- |
| PED | %ΔQd / %ΔP | Magnitude → inelastic vs elastic |
| YED | %ΔQd / %ΔIncome | Positive = normal, negative = inferior |
| XED | %ΔQd of X / %ΔP of Y | Positive = substitutes, negative = complements |
| Revenue test | Δ(P×Q) after price change | TR and price move together when inelastic |

[summary]
Elasticity converts "how sensitive?" into a number: PED for own price,
YED for income (sign classifies the good), XED for related goods (sign
classifies the relationship). Sellers and tax authorities both price
against PED — inelastic goods carry the markups and the sin taxes.
[/summary]
